{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D111-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f870d91132a11afc9608e20dce91c4c765158915e3a83a551ce496dcca446c40\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 hides rejection information, but A1–A5 never establish that B needs hope to continue.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 evades B2's rejection pile; A5 redirects B4's biggest-gallery question toward the unanswered application.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek facts, but B's personal investment in continuing remains unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats A1's packing proposal with a hopeful justification rather than increasing the concealment's consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies paintings and a remaining gallery; B2 makes the rejection pile playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Nothing that helps us pack' economically converts an information request into practical evasion.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let's pack your paintings for the last gallery. You've finally picked up a brush again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"If the big gallery rejected me too, I'm done. Did they write?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Their letter can wait. This gallery still needs your best three.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Pick them, then. I can't face another envelope.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll handle the envelopes. You finish the blue one; there's still somewhere for it to go.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D111 makes A conceal discouraging facts because A believes preserving B's hope is necessary for B to continue.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary encouragement can acknowledge all the bad news; this drive requires protective withholding.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 withholds the pile's contents; revised B2 explicitly links rejection to quitting, and A3 withholds the letter.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses a fellow artist's practical help and control of correspondence; alternative b uses selective reading and a gardening partnership.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision preserves the gallery setting and supplies the missing dependence on hope. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (B2/A3 concealment protects continued painting), logic 5 (A3 answers the letter threat; A5 accepts B4's envelope request), relationship 4 (B4 delegates a painful task), heightening 4 (A5 assumes future correspondence), specificity 4 (A1 paintings, A5 blue canvas), brevity/wit 4 (A3's useful evasion); total 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's protective motive is clear, but withholding another artist's correspondence can feel controlling; performance should preserve sincere concern.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D111-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cfa8ee7e0f4aaa98f1349735069ee3ec198be592773f7d4b9ef2382bdaa63bdc\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 exposes concealment and A3 selectively reads the letter, but B's ability to continue is not at stake.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains the covered letter after B2; A5 evades B4's question about waiting-list length.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 investigate A's evasion without revealing why the garden matters personally.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 substitutes seedling practice for an answer, but adds little consequence to A3's selective disclosure.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's seed packets and B2's partly covered letter provide immediately playable objects.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'useful half' efficiently reveals A's selective definition of useful information.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep the seed packets. The allotment letter says we're on the waiting list.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You've covered our number. If it's another year indoors, I'm giving up gardening.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The important bit is we're on it. Let's start tomatoes on my windowsill.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You'll get tired of them before we get a plot.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Take my sunny room. I'll move the bed; keep the packets.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D111 makes A conceal discouraging facts because A believes preserving B's hope is necessary for B to continue.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Optimistic reframing changes the meaning of known facts; A instead prevents B from learning the discouraging number.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 identifies both the hidden number and the intention to quit, while A3 continues withholding it.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike alternative a's management of rejection letters, b answers distrust with a costly offer of shared growing space.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The allotment setting remains; the revision adds an explicit quitting threshold and a practical sacrifice. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (B2/A3 hidden number), logic 5 (A3 supplies indoor gardening; A5 answers B4's endurance concern), relationship 4 (B4 questions A's commitment), heightening 4 (A5 offers the bedroom), specificity 5 (A3 windowsill tomatoes), brevity/wit 4 (A5's bed displacement follows the offer); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 foregrounds help more than concealment, although the withheld queue position remains the reason this substitute is needed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D112-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b1bcc7a83528004d5d5ea7d6912773e2e00b01f99ebc4fcd4d5e4fd257712661\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 insists B answer first, but A5's tissues only imply A shares B4's hurt.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 resists B2's returned question; A5 changes immediately after B4 admits being hurt.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks reciprocity before B4 voluntarily supplies the admission A needs.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves from guarded questioning to an implied emotional disclosure after B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's unspecified cancellation leaves the event and relationship indistinct.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'precautionary' tissues economically reveal earlier emotional preparation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 82\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"When Mum cancelled our birthday dinner, were you disappointed?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Were you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd like your answer before I give mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Yes. I cried in the supermarket.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Me too. I told the cashier the birthday candles were seasonal allergies.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D112 makes A obtain another person's admission of distress before exposing the matching feeling in A.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Soliciting sympathy starts with one's own distress; this drive delays that disclosure until B goes first.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 explicitly requires B's answer first; revised A5's 'Me too' makes the previously implied shared hurt unmistakable.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses reciprocal questioning between siblings; b uses a colleague's specific admission to unlock a withheld complaint.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision specifies a family cancellation and makes A's matching feeling explicit. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 delays, A5 shares), logic 5 (A3 answers B2, A5 echoes B4's supermarket crying), relationship 4 (B2 requests reciprocity), heightening 4 (A5 reveals a humiliating cover story), specificity 5 (A1 birthday dinner), brevity/wit 4 (A5's candle excuse exposes concealment); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The cashier excuse is deliberately transparent; delivery must make it A's embarrassed admission rather than a standalone joke.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D112-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3917804225f04e5b93b9e74d71de7019828cee107e48a69a6de37e42a3f98e5e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks B's hurt before A5 reveals a complaint, although complaint and shared hurt are not identical.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's motive question; A5 treats B4's admission as permission to disclose.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 is understandably wary, but A1's 'only your face' makes A sound needlessly mocking.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 announces a complaint without revealing any of its emotional substance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names an unspecified joke, leaving the shared injury and setting vague.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'unfold my complaint' supplies a flourish without establishing a literal document or revealing hurt.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Did the boss calling us office furniture hurt you?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why? Are you making a complaint?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It's still in drafts. How did you feel?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Invisible. I've worked here twelve years.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Me too. Mine says 'unprofessional'; I'm changing that to 'I went home and cried.'\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D112 makes A secure a matching emotional admission before risking A's own disclosure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Recruiting support for a grievance needs agreement; this card specifically needs another person's vulnerable feeling first.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 postpones discussing the complaint to ask about feeling, and B4's 'Invisible' unlocks A5's crying admission.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a directly bargains over who answers first; b hides behind a draft complaint until a colleague names the injury.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision introduces a workplace setting and gives the complaint literal and emotional substance. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 conditional disclosure), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's complaint question; A5 uses B4's invisibility), relationship 4 (B2 questions A's purpose), heightening 4 (A5 replaces formal wording with personal exposure), specificity 5 (A1 office-furniture insult), brevity/wit 4 (A5's edit embodies the shift); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 reports an intended disclosure rather than sending the complaint; the scene appropriately leaves that further choice open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D113-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d8f17b02dd355cc52b089ab8f60d3d3884c5bb919cb70cec332ff27512cb0f99\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls rejection the exact needed lesson; A3 and A5 make financial losses necessary lessons in independence and detachment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's need for the contract into a lesson; A5 specifically converts B4's mixer debt into another.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants income and B4 names the loan, giving the bakery partner a concrete stake against A's philosophy.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 moves from lost income to endangered equipment, and A5 extends the growth doctrine to that consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a bakery rejection and B4 supplies a mixer loan with clear practical consequences.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'attachment to equipment' earns its absurdity directly from B4's mixer loan.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That rejection was exactly the lesson our bakery needed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We needed the contract.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And now we've learned not to need one contract.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We can't pay the mixer loan.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A powerful second lesson about attachment to equipment.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D113 makes A describe a particular loss as precisely the experience needed for personal or collective growth.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Finding a silver lining merely identifies a benefit; A claims the damaging experience itself was necessary.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 says 'exactly the lesson' and A5 treats threatened equipment loss as a further necessary lesson.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a imposes growth on a shared business crisis; b applies it to a housemate's attachment and attempted repair.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal reread: the original ratings remain 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92. B4's mixer loan supplies the exact object of A5's next lesson, preserving both causal links and the exact drive.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's detachment can sound sarcastic; the actor must sincerely believe the bakery needs these lessons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D113-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"9c279b6cbb8527a8c05b5cd615ebc3b646c16fbcf0041c040925a7d788551b65\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 frame the mug's loss as growth, but A5 shifts toward judging B's readiness.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's attachment as depth; A5 rejects B4's gluing proposal without developing its particular implications.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 values the mug and B4 proposes repair, while A's relationship to the breakage remains unclear.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's cupboard chapter repeats the growth metaphor instead of finding a new lesson in B4's repair.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's broken mug and B4's glue are simple playable household details.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'truer morning ritual' and A5's 'new chapter' lean on generic self-help language.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm sorry I broke your graduation mug. Losing it is exactly how we learn to let go.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I want to glue it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That urge is why we needed this. We've confused a degree with a drinking vessel.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then give me your graduation mug.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. Losing mine will teach me generosity. We should both drink from jam jars tomorrow.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D113 makes A insist that a specific disappointment is the exact lesson required for growth.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"An excuse for breaking property deflects blame; this drive extends the claimed educational necessity even to A's own loss.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 makes B2's wish to repair evidence of a needed lesson, and A5 accepts B4's demand as A's lesson in generosity.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The bakery alternative keeps A philosophically insulated; the mug alternative lets B require A to participate in the prescribed growth.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision specifies A's responsibility and gives B a consequential counteroffer. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 necessary lessons), logic 5 (repair prompts attachment diagnosis; B4 prompts self-sacrifice), relationship 5 (B4 redirects the cost), heightening 4 (A5 joins the loss), specificity 5 (graduation mugs and jam jars), brevity/wit 4 (A5 applies the doctrine sincerely); total 95.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The unusually neat reciprocal challenge is illustrative; it should not imply that the actual scene must end with shared jam jars.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D114-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"28c53432a134fe1201b546c9e33d1eb61a7c921700b715eee4fb29cb8b171670\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims readiness and A3 borrows B2's breathing, but A5 only renames that same borrowing.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's numbers; A5 answers B4's accusation through the word 'Synchronised.'\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies a technique and B4 detects copying, but B has little independent emotional stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 defends A3's existing technique without borrowing anything newly useful from B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's unspecified results and A3's 'advanced six' leave the situation thin.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's substitution of 'Synchronised' for copying neatly preserves A's claimed expertise.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm ready for our audition results. Why are you breathing like that?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Four in, six out. It stops my hands shaking.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Four in, six out. I like to arrive already regulated.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I also write down who I'll call if I don't get in.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Naturally. Lend me your pen; my support network deserves advance notice.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D114 makes A perform complete readiness while covertly adopting the coping methods supplied by others.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary help-seeking admits a need; A appropriates help while presenting it as evidence of existing preparedness.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 repeats B2's breathing counts as an established practice, and A5 appropriates B4's support-list strategy.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a borrows discreetly from a fellow audition candidate; b borrows increasingly structured support from someone helping with rejection.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision specifies auditions and replaces the copying accusation with another usable coping response. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 adopt both methods under readiness claims), logic 5 (counts then contact list), relationship 4 (B2/B4 share personal coping), heightening 4 (A5 needs a borrowed pen), specificity 5 (auditions and support list), brevity/wit 4 (A5 disguises need as courtesy); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's claim of arriving regulated is conspicuous; the copying should feel anxious and sincere rather than knowingly parodic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D114-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"98efe800ab7bda1105805e5cbeaf48c8959d6c5300d8aad70ca535b69f260d88\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims ownership of water as coping, but A3 and A5 borrow no fresh strategy from B's responses.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains B2's contradiction and A5 answers B4's timing question coherently.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 expose inconsistency but offer no new assistance or personal stake within the exchange.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 reveals the original glass's arrival rather than increasing A's dependence on surrounding coping.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names disappointment and water without establishing what happened or where.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Very responsive of you' supplies a status flourish, but the coping game remains static.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 61\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm completely prepared for this rejection email. Why have you brought water?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Small sips helped when I lost my job.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"My approach exactly. Leave the jug; I prefer a thorough preparation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I had my sister read the email aloud. Want me to?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. I always arrange a reader. Start gently; that's part of my system.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D114 makes A claim emotional self-sufficiency while quietly incorporating each available coping strategy.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Retrospective credit-taking alone concerns ownership; this drive requires the appropriated material to help A cope emotionally.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 offers water for job-loss distress and B4 offers assisted reading; A3 and A5 recast both as A's established system.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a preserves peer equality through imitation; b accepts a helper's escalating involvement while pretending to have arranged it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision introduces a rejection email and gives both B turns distinct coping methods. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 claim supplied methods), logic 5 (jug follows sips, reader follows offer), relationship 4 (B shares experience and volunteers), heightening 4 (A5 delegates encountering the news), specificity 4 (email and jug), brevity/wit 4 (A5's system rationalization); total 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Delegating the reading resembles avoiding a difficult beginning, but A's repeated appropriation of coping methods keeps D114 dominant.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D115-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b4f46568b74e6557cc9061a5b658b0e3116f388f76b19a687c57e80bdd714179\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 makes B's sleepless night subordinate to A's week, and A3 continues claiming emotional priority.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's wish to talk into permission for A's story; A5 explicitly answers B4's contest objection.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asks for listening and B4 sets a boundary against comparison.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's seven nights simply restate A1's week without a new sacrifice, fear, or consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes lost sleep but supplies no cause, relationship, or surrounding situation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'won't seem threatening' exposes the competition A pretends to disavow.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One sleepless night before your interview? I've been awake all week worrying about mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I just need you to practise questions with me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Ask why I left my last job. You'll understand why my interview is harder.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm scared I'll freeze.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm scared I'll cry. Let's use your practice time to get me through the greeting.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D115 makes A answer another person's distress with a personal distress that A treats as more deserving of attention.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Empathic self-disclosure returns attention to the other person; A uses comparison to acquire their listening time.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 takes over B2's interview practice, and A5 uses B4's fear of freezing to claim priority for A's fear of crying.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a disguises taking attention as useful interview practice; b exploits condolences before demanding priority at a shared venue.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision adds interview stakes and gives B4 fresh fear that causes a new comparison. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 redirect attention to worse personal distress), logic 5 (practice becomes A's rehearsal; freezing becomes crying), relationship 4 (B2 has a practical need), heightening 4 (A5 captures the practice time), specificity 5 (interview greeting), brevity/wit 4 (A5's small rehearsal target exposes large need); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A is openly self-centered, so the offer to explain the harder interview needs sincere conviction rather than deliberate bullying.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D115-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c136d7a0ed88de1c7e6293e112a428c4f689993db3149dca01ba4ff9ed559fae\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 outbids B's disappointing opening and A3 solicits more attention for A's smaller audience.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 adds the snack detail after B2's apology but does not meaningfully depend on that apology; A5 answers B4's request.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers sympathy and B4 then tries to reclaim the original conversation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 adds a worse detail, but A5 abstracts the competition into 'scale' instead of increasing its cost.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's two departing audience members and A3's interval snacks create a recognizable theatrical failure.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's stolen snacks are concrete, whereas A5's 'how disappointing can scale' sounds editorial.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your opening had empty seats? Mine had two people, and both left.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm sorry. Have my complimentary drink.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. My theatre couldn't even afford to console us.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can you listen now? My dad left before my scene.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Mine asked for a refund. Could you stay while I finish this? I haven't told anyone that.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D115 makes A repeatedly present a personal disappointment as the one that warrants the room's attention.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sharing comparable experience can offer solidarity; A's comparisons consistently postpone hearing B.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 converts B2's offered drink into evidence of A's worse theatre, and A5 counters B4's parental hurt with a refund demand.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a seizes a practical rehearsal; b accepts comfort and then converts a fellow performer's personal disclosure into another claim on care.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The theatre setting remains, with a drink making B2 causally useful and parental hurt sharpening B4. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 worse personal disappointments), logic 5 (drink comparison then father comparison), relationship 4 (B offers help then asks to be heard), heightening 4 (A5 moves from attendance to parental rejection), specificity 5 (complimentary drink and refund), brevity/wit 4 (A3 exploits the actual offered comfort); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The matching father stories are compactly convenient; A5's admission should carry real hurt rather than merely a competitive punchline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D116-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2a3f6624cf74f2c56fb4f33538f13f6fcfff8714952b1712bb16b37a16f136a5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 delays hope until Monday, but A3's different letter does not identify a redirected route to any specific desired outcome.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's permanent refusal; A5 avoids B4's 'From whom?' with unspecified surprise.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 tests the refusal and B4 requests a source, but neither speaker's concrete investment is established.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 offers less concrete commitment than A3's replacement letter.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 never identifies who refused what, and A5 leaves the desired result equally unknown.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's Monday surprise is compact but detachable from any particular disappointment.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 55\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The hall rejected our wedding booking. Apparently we're meant to marry somewhere less municipal.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Every venue is booked for June.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then September gives us three more months to practise being married.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"My parents can't travel in September.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we go to them. Their garden! We're finally finding out where this wedding belongs.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D116 makes each disappointment become a reason the same desired outcome is taking a different or more meaningful route.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D113 treats loss itself as necessary growth; D116 preserves pursuit of the desired outcome by relocating its fulfillment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 moves the wedding date after B2, and A5 moves its location after B4 while preserving the wedding goal.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a changes timing and family location under logistical pressure; b welcomes a partner's smaller commercial format as the dream's next form.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision introduces a wedding-booking setting because the original supplies no identifiable goal. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 delay, A5 meaningful redirection), logic 5 (June shortage then parental travel limit), relationship 4 (B protects feasibility and family attendance), heightening 4 (A5 relocates the wedding), specificity 5 (June, September, parents' garden), brevity/wit 4 (A1's municipal destiny follows the refusal); total 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The garden is a hopeful proposal, not an established available venue; further practical resistance remains possible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D116-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ecf04667880f9e7bc52af0e78a9f7217499d446bbafe0f4e3eb69c445a0b8866\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 redirects the failed shop geographically, A3 shrinks its format after financial disappointment, and A5 gives that redirection meaning.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3's smaller address directly uses B2's lack of moving money; A5 adopts B4's market-stall proposal.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 guards the shared budget and B4 helps find a viable smaller expression of the shop.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 promotes B4's compromise into a positive new identity for the dream.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a failed shop and B4 supplies a market stall, though the business type is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'travel light' follows the physical downsizing proposed in B4.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our bookshop failed here. We're meant to find readers somewhere else.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We have no moving money.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we're meant to start smaller. One shelf, properly chosen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I could get us a market stall beside the bus stop.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"People waiting with nothing to read! I'll pack the short stories. We've been making our customers come too far.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D116 makes A reinterpret setbacks as delays or redirections of a still-living desired outcome.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple problem-solving finds a cheaper option; A additionally treats each restriction as hopeful development of the dream.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 treats B2's lack of money as a reason for a smaller beginning; A5 treats B4's bus-stop stall as discovery of the bookshop's intended readers.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a redirects a wedding under successive family constraints; b uses a business partner's helpful proposal to commit to a more purposeful version of the failed shop.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the rejected abstract endorsement into a concrete next expression of hope, specifying a bookshop and bus-stop market stall. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3's 'meant' and A5's discovered customers reinterpret setbacks), logic 5 (B2 reduces scale; B4 determines A5's short-story stock), relationship 4 (B2 protects funds and B4 offers access), heightening 4 (A5 commits to packing and redefines the failure), specificity 5 (A1 bookshop, B4 bus stop), brevity/wit 4 (A5 makes waiting passengers the desired readership); total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; causal and other hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The bus-stop readership is A's hopeful inference, not demonstrated demand. The proposal remains open to B's practical knowledge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D117-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"260694ca3aa7ebedf90b4f0077cb23692440d5976ec698c4b0be94311f893fe0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 conceals a possible tear-soaked sleeve, but A5's tea concern does not make A's distress harder to hide.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's sleeve observation and A5 defers B4's invitation to consider sitting.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 notices A's condition and B4 tries to redirect care toward A.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a tea condition without intensifying the visible distress suggested by B2.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's bad day is vague, though B2's sleeve and A5's tea provide domestic objects.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Your day was saying something' feels constructed, and A5's comforting temperature adds abstraction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've brought tissues. Being laid off together doesn't make your day any easier.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're wiping your eyes on your sleeve.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm saving the soft ones for you. Tell me what you're worried about.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You. You can't even get the tissue box open.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then take the whole box. I'll make tea once my hands stop doing this.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D117 makes A intensify care for someone else while A's own distress increasingly escapes concealment.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Selfless caretaking can remain emotionally steady; this card requires the caregiver's own pain to become harder to hide.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 identifies tears, B4 identifies impaired hands, and A5 keeps giving comfort while finally acknowledging the shaking.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a makes care physically harder as distress becomes visible; b uses a friend's reciprocal offer to trigger an admission inside further caretaking.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected the rejected candidate's tissue continuity: A1 now brings tissues without implying that the unopened box has already dispensed them. The shared-layoff setting and remaining dialogue are preserved. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 reserves comfort for B while A5 exposes shaking), logic 5 (B2 prompts the soft-tissue excuse; B4 prompts handing over the unopened box), relationship 4 (B4 redirects concern toward A), heightening 4 (A5 offers the whole box and tea despite impaired hands), specificity 5 (A1 layoffs and B4 unopened box), brevity/wit 4 (A3's tissue rationing rationalizes self-neglect); total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 depends on B4 making the hand difficulty audible; the comedy remains tender and rests on A's persistent practical care.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D117-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"230f35da69e1ca5daaa6a2ed3529de6875293dbcd418f069bf8a930409223547\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses shared disappointment to justify soup, but A5 shows no increasing difficulty hiding A's distress.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's shared letter as qualification, and A5 delays B4's offer to eat.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 recognizes shared pain and B4 offers reciprocal care through the soup.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats other-first service without raising the intensity of comfort or exposure.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies soup, but B2's disappointing letter leaves the actual loss unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's soup qualification and A5's quality control turn caretaking into a compact protective procedure.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've made you soup. The choir rejecting us doesn't mean you should miss dinner.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You've set a bowl for yourself too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"So you won't have to eat alone. I'll butter your bread.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sit with me. I don't want you crying in the kitchen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"All right. But take my bread too. I can't swallow yet, and you shouldn't have to ask twice.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D117 makes A respond to pain with increasing comfort for B while A's own suffering becomes unmistakable.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding one's feelings through chores is adjacent, but the precise behavior directs progressively more care toward another hurt person.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explains A's own bowl as company for B; after B4 names crying, A5 admits being unable to swallow while giving B more food.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a exposes distress through failing hands; b lets a friend's request for company bring A's hidden distress into the shared meal.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision specifies choir rejection and turns B4's reciprocal comfort into the cause of A5's exposed distress. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 care intensifies as concealment fails), logic 5 (second bowl becomes company; invitation prompts sitting and admission), relationship 5 (B4 wants A present), heightening 4 (A5