],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D118 makes A treat emotional exposure or care as an investment that creates a claim to comparable emotional risk.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A request for mutual openness need not establish a debt; A evaluates B's disclosure as repayment for A's prior risk.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 declares an emotional debt; after B4 supplies a private fear, A5 requires the same audience to make its exposure equal to A's.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a demands equivalent exposure to a partner's mother and tightens the repayment terms; b allows delayed repayment but negotiates a concrete future vulnerability.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the rejected candidate's closing reassurance into a further demand for equal risk. The family-lunch setting remains, with A's earlier disclosure now explicitly made to B's mother. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 debt and A5 audience equivalence), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's unsolicited-disclosure objection; A5 evaluates B4's particular fear), relationship 4 (B2 contests the obligation and B4 risks jealousy), heightening 4 (A5 raises private disclosure to exposure before the mother), specificity 5 (A1 Sunday and A5 lunch audience), brevity/wit 4 (A5's exact matching follows A's emotional accounting); total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's demand is intrusive and may sound punitive; its motive must remain a sincere belief that comparable exposure proves reciprocal investment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D118-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d2c6a5f9f5f1cadf5e9cc337663a5940123bf30bbcf52e6ca39a0f760889928a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 conditions emotional support on future equal openness, and A5 explicitly credits B's uncertainty as a first payment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's scorekeeping challenge; A5 converts B4's inability into a payable piece of honesty.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions the arrangement and B4 admits a limit that makes A accept a smaller immediate return.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends the investment logic by treating an apparent obstacle as an initial installment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's hard conversation is unspecified, though the request to stay supplies a playable immediate interaction.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'first payment' reveals the bookkeeping concealed beneath A3's softer language.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll stay while you pack his clothes. Someday I need you to let me see you fall apart too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Does comforting me come with a bill?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You saw me cry through my divorce. I need equal trust eventually.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can talk. I can't promise tears.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then tell me which shirt you're keeping. That can count; you always pretend you want nothing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D118 makes emotional support an investment for which A expects eventual repayment through equal vulnerability.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Unconditional support accepts B's limits without crediting a return; A converts even a limit into partial payment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explicitly requires equal trust in return for A's prior exposure; A5 accepts B4's offer to talk by identifying a personally risky admission that can count.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a requires matching exposure before a partner's mother; b bargains within a friend's stated limit, translating desired tears into an admission of attachment.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the rejected abstraction with a friend helping pack a former partner's clothes. B4 now offers speech instead of guaranteed tears, so A5 requests a new, concrete admission rather than repetition of B's uncertainty. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 equal trust, A5 credited disclosure), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's bill objection; A5 converts B4's offer into the shirt question), relationship 4 (B4 sets a credible limit), heightening 4 (A5 turns general repayment into admitting a concealed attachment), specificity 4 (A1 clothes and A3 divorce ground the encounter, though B's separation is inferred), brevity/wit 4 (A5's 'That can count' makes accounting personal); total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The request could resemble compassionate encouragement on its own; A3's explicit equivalence and A5's credit language are necessary to retain the transactional drive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D119-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f746b471ebd303e45a7ecf2869d1fcac4e9df8d5f620baf83dc190a7dbe1882d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees to discuss one argument under a scope limit; A3 and A5 explicitly preserve the ability to remain and pause.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 acknowledges B2's whole-year concern while limiting capacity; A5 answers B4's starting-point question with topic and safety condition.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the broader history recognized, then B4 cooperates in finding a manageable start.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds permission to pause but mostly consolidates A1's existing boundary.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an argument discussion tonight, and A3's risk of leaving makes the immediate limit playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's single sentence and A5's permission to pause express the emotional condition without explanatory padding.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 87\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll talk about last night's rent argument, but not the whole year tonight.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The whole year matters. You've been pulling away.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It does. One question, and let me finish before you answer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"All right. Were you going to move out?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I packed a bag. It's still upstairs. Please let that be the whole answer for a minute.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D119 makes A agree to emotional openness only within conditions that preserve A's sense of safety.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoidance refuses engagement; A offers a limited, feasible form of engagement and specifies the protection it requires.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 limits the exchange to one uninterrupted answer; after B4 accepts and asks about departure, A5 admits packing a bag while requesting time before further discussion.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a protects a difficult admission through scope and pacing limits; b uses exit access and stopping permission to disclose a wish for reconciliation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the rejected ending so protected openness occurs in speech. Added a rent argument and possible move to the existing year-long dispute. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 preserve safety while answering), logic 5 (B2's larger concern prompts one-question terms; B4's accepted terms and departure question cause A5's bag admission), relationship 4 (B2 seeks the broader truth and B4 accommodates limits), heightening 4 (A5 reveals an actual preparation to leave), specificity 5 (A1 rent and A5 upstairs bag), brevity/wit 3 (A5 is direct and playable but lightly comic); total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. Downstream attribution remains separately unresolved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The scene is primarily emotionally tense rather than comic. Its revised transcript cannot replace the supplied versioned seed snapshot without a separate provenance decision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D119-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"dc9c52cbee2e885e67063fbae288bdfb4037daf4d68c9e48a6a1c2d3d94c9788\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explicitly makes the ability to leave the condition for staying, and A5 risks greater honesty after B4 supplies safety.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 corrects B2's interpretation of the door seat; A5 directly uses B4's permission to stop.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 fears departure and B4 responds with an accommodation that changes A's willingness to speak.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 advances from arranging a safe seat to risking a less guarded answer because of B4.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's door-side seat provides a concrete safety condition, though the conversation's topic remains open.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Knowing I can leave is helping me stay' expresses the character's paradox directly and economically.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll sit by the door while we talk about trying again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B